    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d261-a1">

                <pb facs="0731" n="609" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg609"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    139—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mariscal to Mr. Whitehouse.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1889-10-07"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 7,
                        1889</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chargé</hi>, etc.:</p>
                <p>Referring to the legation’s note of 17th August last, relative to the
                    disagreeable incidents which occurred in Eagle Pass on the 3d March, 1888, I
                    have the honor to advise you that I have received through the War Department a
                    copy of the sentence pronounced by the supreme court of military justice on the
                    charges brought against the first captain, Francisco A. Muños, and others,
                    responsible for the incidents.</p>
                <p>Inclosed I send you a copy of the said sentence, advising you that in case you
                    have instructions to take part in the conference requested by Mr. Ryan you can
                    do so whenever you wish.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ignacio Mariscal.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
